Parts of the plan reconciliation rules (identity and lifecycle protection, append-only
event history, editorial/semantic classification), the Markdown task and event patterns,
the sprint template and the idempotent finish phase machine are derived from the author's
private Project Tracker Next (part of the private Agent Platform Next). Private paths,
hosts and data were removed.

Ideas (no code) were taken from: dunnit (MIT; anti-gaming diff checks), BMAD TEA (MIT;
gate decision separated from waivers), OpenSpec (MIT; ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED item diff
vocabulary) and the Claude Code hook protocol (host documentation).
